-- E6, no accidental handling (SPEC §19 Laws item 3, the kernel program `tunnel`; SPEC §29):
-- `fwrap` runs its block under its own handler of `Fail`, `default(false)`. The block raises
-- `Fail`, and it is written under `to_result`: its raise goes to the handler around it where it is
-- written, and passes `fwrap`'s, whose static name is its own site's. `fwrap`'s copy at the
-- block's row, `fwrap__b0n2`, handles its own site 3 and performs the block's site 2.
--
-- Answer: `inr ()`: the error, at `to_result` (`default`'s `false` would be `inl inl ()`);
-- `live 0`.

include fail

fn fwrap(g: !(1 => bool)) -> bool = with default[1, bool](false) { g(()) }

main -> bool + 1 = with to_result[1, bool] { fwrap(!{ u -> raise(()) }) }
